From 2764e93f8cdc5018fceadf0e564c7026be268558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:02:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 19/22] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7125-samsung: enable GPI DMA
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Some of the QUP serial engines (e.g. the touchscreen I2C at a84000)
are set up by the firmware for GSI/GPI DMA mode, and geni-i2c then
fails to probe without a DMA channel ("Failed to get tx DMA ch").

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi
index 90bcab5921c0..5ee0ad9e6d7a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi
@@ -383,6 +383,14 @@ vreg_bob: bob {
 	};
 };
 
+&gpi_dma0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&gpi_dma1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &ipa {
 	memory-region = <&ipa_fw_mem>;
 };
-- 
2.55.0

